How do you handle the drift in terraform?

Terraform drift happens when the real infrastructure in the cloud is different from what Terraform thinks it is.

In interviews you can say like this-

Terraform drift occurs when the actual infrastructure differs from the Terraform state or configuration, usually due to manual changes or external systems. We detect drift using terraform plan or -refresh-only. To handle it, we either let Terraform reconcile the infrastructure, update code to match reality, or explicitly ignore expected changes using lifecycle rules. In production, we prevent drift through CI/CD pipelines, remote state, locking, and strict no-manual-change policies.

